WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.980
[NARRATOR] Gold Roger,
the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.980
attained every treasure that
the world had to offer.

4
00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.720
Smiling, even as he stood
upon the scaffold,

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.090
he issued a challenge
to the world.

6
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.320
[GOLD ROGER]
You want my treasure?

7
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.420
You can have it!

8
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.160
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

9
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.530
Now you just have to find it!

10
00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.500
[NARRATOR]
Now, those who dare to dream

11
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.500
hoist their flags and sail
into the Great Pirate Era!

12
00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.500
[tense orchestral music]

13
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.860
Have you lost your mind, Luffy?

14
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:03.870
<b>Adventure in the Deep Sea</b>

15
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.730
[LUFFY]
Well, if we catch it, we can
teach it how to pull the ship!

16
00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.930
[USOPP]
Like hell we can!

17
00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.730
I'd tell you to take a good look
at it, but it's so ridiculously huge,

18
00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.020
I don't know how in the world
you could miss the damn thing!

19
00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.260
Yeah, that is big.

20
00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.050
We're all gonna die!

21
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.390
[USOPP]
It must've been here for centuries!

22
00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.210
The kraken shows up in myths
from all over the world!

23
00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:22.530
It's one of the most terrible
monsters that ever lived!

24
00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:27.450
It doesn't have any bones,
and I am only bones...

25
00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:28.450
That's interesting.

26
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.950
I wonder if it enjoys
making no-skull jokes.

27
00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:33.550
Yeah, I doubt it!

28
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.300
[playful orchestral music]

29
00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:35.820
[FRANKY]
Hey, you're a pretty good artist.

30
00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.030
I wanted to capture
the moment on paper.

31
00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:40.060
Drawing pictures?! Really?!

32
00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:43.460
I'll help you out.
You've got a plan, right?

33
00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.030
Problem is, there's not
much we can do underwater.

34
00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:49.400
No. No. No.

35
00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.810
The problem is,
the thing's gigantic.

36
00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.540
We couldn't even take it
on above sea level.

37
00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.150
[CARIBOU]
What is wrong with these people?

38
00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.980
Anybody in their right mind
would've run for the hills by now!

39
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.490
What's taking them
so long to decide?

40
00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.990
We're leaving!
Shift the helm due south!

41
00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:09.650
Hey, Nami! Let's go
straight toward it!

42
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:11.360
[NAMI]
Don't be stupid! That thing is...

43
00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:15.190
[SANJI]
It's okay, Nami. I'm here for y...

44
00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:17.160
Here for...

45
00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.300
...for you.

46
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.040
You held it in! Good job!

47
00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.470
We made him all better!

48
00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.970
Well, it helps that Nami
put on a coat, too.

49
00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.710
[CARIBOU]
I'm not safe on this ship.

50
00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:31.600
I'll have to protect myself.

51
00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:34.110
Somethin's coming up behind us.

52
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.280
[SURUME roars]

53
00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:36.480
Huh?

54
00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.990
[CORIBOU]
Brother!

55
00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.320
[USOPP]
These guys again?

56
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.320
Ah! I'm so happy you
came back for me!

57
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.760
Let's rush in there
and rescue my bro!

58
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.230
[CARIBOU PIRATES]
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

59
00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.330
You're the best crew
a captain could ask for!

60
00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:58.400
Stop it!

61
00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.070
[CHOPPER, USOPP, BROOK scream]

62
00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.010
[CHOPPER]
It destroyed the coating!

63
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:06.300
[USOPP]
That ship's bigger than the Sunny! [dramatic orchestral music]

64
00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.850
No! They didn't make it!

65
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.590
[CARIBOU cries]

66
00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.630
Like jellyfish.

67
00:04:21.630 --> 00:04:24.630
Dammit, Roronoa!
That's too cruel!

68
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.230
[USOPP]
Here it comes!

69
00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.070
It's so huge!

70
00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.970
There's no way we can fight
against a monster like that!

71
00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.010
Now, Third Gear...

72
00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.540
No!

73
00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:41.480
If you do that, you'll break
the bubble for sure!

74
00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:47.020
Chicken... Voyage!

75
00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.620
Can't we... Ah!... escape somehow?

76
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.090
Wait, let me take care of it.

77
00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.230
Don't go!

78
00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.490
If you pop the bubble,
then we all die!

79
00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.100
The little fellow's right!

80
00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.600
But if you wanna face
the kraken that badly,

81
00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.050
I might just have
the idea for you!

82
00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:05.810
Fine, what is it?
Make it snappy!

83
00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.410
There! Perfect!

84
00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.510
That contraption is called
the Flutter Kick Coating.

85
00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.250
It's an extravehicular
diving suit.

86
00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:16.150
As long as you stay inside it,

87
00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:19.250
you can fight underwater
as much as you need to.

88
00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.840
Pretty amazing, right?

89
00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.090
[CARIBOU]
If I let them call the shots, we'll
all go to hell in a handbasket.

90
00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.330
Hey, you weren't
supposed to do that!

91
00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.860
The rest of us wanted
to get out of here!

92
00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:32.200
Now they're gonna stay and
try to fight that thing!

93
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.030
I've been telling you all to run
away from the beginning,

94
00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:38.020
but your fearless leader was
having none of that, now was he?

95
00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:41.140
Think of it this way, would you
rather have them fight it outside

96
00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.940
or fight it right here
on the ship?

97
00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.840
Right! You guys get out there!

98
00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:45.780
Far, far away!

99
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.300
[upbeat electronic music]

100
00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.310
This rope's kinda annoying.

101
00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.950
Remember to stay as far
from the ship as you can!

102
00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.850
Sure.

103
00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.490
Well, you ready?

104
00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.520
Yeah!

105
00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.120
Huh? Wait a sec!

106
00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.340
You guys forgot
the safety ropes!

107
00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:03.160
You're gonna get separated!

108
00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:06.200
Sounds like Nami's
worried about me.

109
00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.670
Listen up!

110
00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.740
I need both of you guys
to distract him.

111
00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:12.170
If I can get one good punch off,
I think I can take him!

112
00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.140
Why don't I just slice him
to pieces? It'd be easier.

113
00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.190
'Cause that wouldn't
do me any good!

114
00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:20.310
I wanna capture him
and keep him as a pet!

115
00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.050
[CHOPPER]
Careful, guys.

116
00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.920
Yeah, and keep your distance!
'Cause every centimeter counts.

117
00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.460
[BOTH scream]

118
00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.820
[USOPP]
Okay, that was way too close!

119
00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:33.300
All right, stand back!

120
00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.900
Franky...

121
00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.210
[BOTH gasping]

122
00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.790
[gasps]

123
00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.500
...Rocket Launcher!

124
00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.300
[dramatic orchestral music]

125
00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.500
[USOPP]
Got 'im!

126
00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.330
[CHOPPER]
That was incredible!

127
00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.410
[BOTH scream]

128
00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.770
Not another one!

129
00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:50.480
How many arms does it have?

130
00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.960
It's gonna hit us!

131
00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.530
Guard Point!

132
00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:57.470
Whoa! It hit the ship pretty hard!

133
00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:00.710
[CHOPPER]
Everyone okay?

134
00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.140
[USOPP]
He... He saved us!

135
00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:04.180
Thanks, buddy!

136
00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.150
Nice one, Chopper!

137
00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:11.040
We're about to be
crushed against that mountain!

138
00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.140
[gasps] Now, Mil Fleurs!

139
00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.640
Gigantesco Mano!

140
00:07:16.670 --> 00:07:19.710
[ALL screaming]

141
00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.480
Wow, those hands are big!

142
00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:23.580
[gasps]

143
00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.060
– [FRANKY] Yeah!
– [CHOPPER] Woo-hoo!

144
00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.790
Nice one, Robin!
That was close!

145
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.040
[BROOK laughing]

146
00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.260
Thank goodness.

147
00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.770
I was only in the water
for the briefest moment,

148
00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:35.750
so my power held out.

149
00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:39.220
Now, guess it's my turn!

150
00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.360
Third Gear.

151
00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:03.880
Armament Hardening!

152
00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.350
What the hell is that?

153
00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.200
So tough underwater.

154
00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.570
Come on!

155
00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:16.320
Aw, crap!

156
00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:18.770
Doesn't look like that octopus
is gonna wait patiently.

157
00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:20.740
Blue Walk!

158
00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:23.890
Oh, my. Sanji just
left his bubble!

159
00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.870
He's fast even in the sea!

160
00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.890
Like a Fishman! So cool!

161
00:08:28.890 --> 00:08:33.080
I spent two years running
from those monsters on that island.

162
00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:36.990
And the first thing I do is
run straight at another one.

163
00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.870
But all things considered,
this one's a bit cuter, really.

164
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:40.300
[tense orchestral music]

165
00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:43.000
Diable Jambe!

166
00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:51.040
Bien Cuit... Grill Shoot!

167
00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:58.880
[roars]

168
00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:04.260
Three-Sword Style...
Crossing the Six Paths!

169
00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:16.300
Hey, were you two
not listenin' to me?!

170
00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.780
I told you not to cut it!

171
00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:23.010
My turn! Gum-Gum...

172
00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.890
...Elephant Gun!

173
00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:31.740
[yelling]

174
00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.390
[grunts]

175
00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.100
He blew it away!

176
00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.080
[NAMI gasps]

177
00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:37.250
What kind of training did
Luffy go through?

178
00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.160
Hm? What the...?

179
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.130
You guys see that?

180
00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.910
[OTHERS]
Huh?

181
00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.610
[NAMI]
It's a shark.

182
00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.000
Huh.

183
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.240
Yeah, why is that
shark wearing a shirt?

184
00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.070
Not to mention it's huge.

185
00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:00.300
[urgent percussion music]

186
00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.840
[LUFFY yelling]

187
00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:14.870
They're being swept away
by the downward current!

188
00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.420
[USOPP]
We can't get split up
down here! Follow them!

189
00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.420
[FRANKY]
Right!

190
00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:21.730
[STRAW HATS screaming]

191
00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:24.360
[CHOPPER]
I don't wanna die down
here! It's dark and wet!

192
00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:25.930
[CARIBOU]
Would you fools pull it together?!

193
00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:26.830
[FRANKY]
Forgot that dude was here.

194
00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.130
Why aren't you panicking?!

195
00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:29.500
[CHOPPER screaming]

196
00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:30.800
[BROOK]
If I had a stomach,

197
00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:33.440
I would be voiding its
contents right now!

198
00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.980
Keep the yard level, Franky!

199
00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.390
Turn hard to port!

200
00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:42.740
Otherwise, we're gonna crash!

201
00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.650
All right, I'm on it!

202
00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:47.690
[NAMI]
Don't let up for a second
or the ship's a goner!

203
00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:52.180
Let's keep it
together, everybody!

204
00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.550
Stay in the center
of the current!

205
00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:57.390
Doin' my best!

206
00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.430
[FRANKY]
It's way too fast!

207
00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:05.000
[LUFFY laughs]

208
00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:06.870
This is awesome!

209
00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:15.980
[laughing]

210
00:11:19.140 --> 00:11:20.040
You're awake.

211
00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:22.580
Ah! What a headache!

212
00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:23.940
[USOPP sighs]

213
00:11:23.980 --> 00:11:26.150
But at least we made it.

214
00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.300
[subdued orchestral music]

215
00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.180
Hm?

216
00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:32.730
What's wrong? Why're you
all making such long faces?

217
00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:36.470
I mean, I'm awake now, so
there's nothing for you to fear!

218
00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.200
[USOPP]
Man, is it freezing!

219
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:44.370
Luffy, Zoro, and Sanji have gone
missing. They're lost in the sea.

220
00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.340
[USOPP]
What?

221
00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:49.540
The best we can do now is hope
the monster didn't tear them apart.

222
00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:51.790
[USOPP]
Glad you're being optimistic.

223
00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.230
[USOPP]
How are we supposed to find them

224
00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:55.490
when we can't even see
what's in front of us?

225
00:11:55.490 --> 00:11:57.780
[BROOK]
I don't like being in the dark.

226
00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:01.260
It feels like something could
attack us from any direction.

227
00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:05.080
[FRANKY]
The best I can guess is we've
descended about 7,000 meters.

228
00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:08.250
Even the Shark Submerge can't
sustain this level of pressure.

229
00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.590
[CHOPPER]
How close are we
to Fishman Island?

230
00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.430
Maybe the others have
already made it there!

231
00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.760
[ROBIN]
Probably not.

232
00:12:14.760 --> 00:12:18.800
According to Camie, it's
10,000 meters below sea level.

233
00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:21.600
[CHOPPER]
And we have 3,000 more to go?

234
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.200
Those guys each have
a bubble and that's all!

235
00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:28.170
Even if they are somehow still
alive, they'll need more air!

236
00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:30.840
None of this would've happened
if they used the safety ropes!

237
00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:32.950
Freakin' out's not helping.

238
00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.310
So let's get to work.

239
00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.150
We can look for 'em
with my new searchlight.

240
00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.550
Whoa!

241
00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:41.310
Does it shine from your eyes?

242
00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:42.910
You'll see.

243
00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:43.650
[gasps]

244
00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.100
[chuckles]

245
00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.410
[FRANKY]
Franky Nipple Lights!

246
00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.520
Why did they have to be there?

247
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.300
[frantic orchestral music]

248
00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.910
[STRAW HATS screaming]

249
00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:56.040
[FRANKY]
Let's get outta here!

250
00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:07.730
Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!

251
00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.300
[mysterious woodwind music]

252
00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:10.440
Where in the world
have you guys gone?

253
00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.580
We need you all back!

254
00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:15.360
This place is so vast,
and we're so far down,

255
00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.640
Sunny's eyes are
practically useless.

256
00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:20.350
[BROOK]
I feel so helpless.

257
00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:24.350
We can barely see. It's no
wonder that everyone is on edge.

258
00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.890
There's gotta be a better
way to tackle this.

259
00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:29.470
You ladies got any ideas?

260
00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:31.620
Keep searching and
just hope for the best.

261
00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.780
We can't stop the ship right now.

262
00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:39.360
[CHOPPER]
Uh! Look, a jellyfish!

263
00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.010
It's like we're inside it!

264
00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:45.160
It's huge! It feels like
it could swallow us whole!

265
00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.670
And they're twinkling!

266
00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.650
It's like a starry sky,
wherever they go!

267
00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:52.430
[gasps] They're so beautiful!

268
00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:54.840
Whoa. That's one long tentacle.

269
00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:57.320
You, uh, wanna shake
hands and be friends?

270
00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.700
Whatever you do, don't touch it!
It's probably venomous!

271
00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.200
[screams]

272
00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.300
[tense orchestral music]

273
00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.640
Aw, crap!

274
00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:10.810
No choice! Coup de Burst!

275
00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.550
No way!

276
00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:17.650
It ate that big jellyfish whole!

277
00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:21.620
Uh. Not to mention, we lost
some air in that maneuver.

278
00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.460
[FRANKY]
It was better than the alternative!

279
00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:24.400
Huh?

280
00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:25.580
But, yeah.

281
00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:28.390
The Coup de Burst sucks
in air to make a quick launch.

282
00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:33.220
Thing is, 'cause we're underwater,
its only resource is our air supply.

283
00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:37.090
So obviously, when we use it,
our bubble shrinks a bit.

284
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.300
[ominous orchestral music]

285
00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.740
[screams]

286
00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:43.270
The fish that attacked it
turned upside down!

287
00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.110
[ROBIN]
A neurotoxin. I figured as much.

288
00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.110
Huh?!

289
00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:50.310
It's awful down here!
And dark! It's scary!

290
00:14:50.310 --> 00:14:55.290
All these creepy creatures
with their freaky eyes!

291
00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.120
Because the sea's so dark,

292
00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:04.690
many of the animals that live
down here have poor eyesight.

293
00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:06.270
[CHOPPER, USOPP sigh]

294
00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:08.920
[CHOPPER]
So they can't see
any better than us.

295
00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:13.100
Hey! Losers! Where ya lookin'?

296
00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:16.270
[ROBIN]
However, there are some that have
highly developed eyes as well.

297
00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.300
[playful harpsichord music]

298
00:15:16.290 --> 00:15:18.730
[CHOPPER, USOPP screaming]

299
00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:23.090
Oh? You're curious as to how I
can see when I don't have eyes?

300
00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:24.300
Of course you are.

301
00:15:24.300 --> 00:15:26.570
But do you really want
to know the answer?

302
00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:29.010
Drum roll!

303
00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.810
[imitates drumming]

304
00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:33.550
It's a secret!

305
00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:37.020
Hey, Brook. Why is it you're
always talkin' to yourself?

306
00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:40.880
It's a habit that comes
from being lonely.

307
00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:43.560
Enough! Quit fooling around!

308
00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:44.230
– [thud]
– [BROOK grunts]

309
00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:44.930
– [thud]
– [USOPP grunts]

310
00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:46.200
– [thud]
– [CHOPPER grunts]

311
00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:48.200
No more violence, please.

312
00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.800
[BOTH]
– Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!
– Luffy! Zoro! Sanji!

313
00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:55.510
[BOTH]
– Help us. Nami is scary.
– Help us. Nami is scary.

314
00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:57.300
[mysterious orchestral music]

315
00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.610
[BROOK]
What's this?

316
00:15:57.610 --> 00:15:59.580
Well, that's not good.

317
00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:01.110
Hey, guys?

318
00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:02.450
[FRANKY]
Huh?

319
00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:05.520
[BROOK]
Have any of you seen the pirate
who boarded the ship?

320
00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:09.950
[FRANKY]
Oh, yeah, I forgot about him. I'm
sure he's around here somewhere.

321
00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.390
[CHOPPER]
But where is somewhere?

322
00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:14.520
I haven't seen him for a while.
Not since we descended.

323
00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:17.640
[CHOPPER]
Do you think he might've been thrown
off when everything went crazy?

324
00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.690
Totally possible. I mean,
his arms and legs were tied up.

325
00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:22.270
There's no way he could
hold on to anything

326
00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.640
while we were rockin' around.

327
00:16:23.640 --> 00:16:26.060
[BROOK]
Normally, I'd agree.

328
00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:28.700
But it seems that he
freed himself. Look.

329
00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:29.370
[CHOPPER, USOPP]
– Huh?!
– Huh?!

330
00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.380
[chuckles]

331
00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:36.070
[USOPP]
So that drippy weirdo
escaped and he's... still here.

332
00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.780
He's gotta be waiting
for the right moment to attack.

333
00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.190
[screams]

334
00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:42.130
This is bad.

335
00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.110
[chuckles]

336
00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.730
[CARIBOU]
If you're so eager to see me,

337
00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:48.150
I'd be happy to sneak into your
room tonight, sweetheart.

338
00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.560
Damn it! We got enough problems.

339
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.300
[ominous string music]

340
00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:53.400
We don't need this guy givin' us
one more thing to worry about!

341
00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:54.880
Don't get worked up.

342
00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.690
It's not like he's an actual
threat to any of us.

343
00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.930
[chuckles]

344
00:16:58.940 --> 00:17:01.320
[CARIBOU]
That's right, you think that.

345
00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:04.070
You'll see how wrong you are
now that the three morons

346
00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:07.180
who could put up a fight have
gotten themselves killed

347
00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:10.360
fighting that kraken.

348
00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:12.640
After all, there's no
way they've survived

349
00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.820
getting sucked down into
the bowels of the ocean

350
00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.630
with just those tiny bubbles
to protect them.

351
00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:19.740
[CARIBOU]
Oh, what a shame that
I didn't have the chance

352
00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:22.350
to kill Straw Hat
with my own hands.

353
00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:24.360
But no one will ever
doubt that he's dead

354
00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:27.210
once I come back with the rest
of his crew members' heads

355
00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:29.760
in tow as my personal trophies.

356
00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:30.920
No one at all.

357
00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:33.370
[CARIBOU laughs]

358
00:17:33.380 --> 00:17:37.270
[CARIBOU]
Mm-hmm. But I can't get too
excited. There's no need to rush.

359
00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:40.890
If I killed them all now, there wouldn't
be anyone left to sail the ship,

360
00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.500
and then what would I do?

361
00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:46.560
So I'll let them live for now, while
they can still be useful to me.

362
00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:49.070
Once we land on Fishman
Island, though,

363
00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:52.340
I'm gonna slaughter you
down to the last man.

364
00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:54.690
[CARIBOU laughs]

365
00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.910
I found him, guys!

366
00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:02.120
[CARIBOU]
Hey! Knock it off, dammit!

367
00:18:02.150 --> 00:18:04.620
I wasn't doing
anything bad, I swear!

368
00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:06.220
Let's see him break outta that.

369
00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:08.820
How did he even manage
to get in there?

370
00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.930
Because we weren't
paying attention to him.

371
00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:13.700
If he weren't so stupid,
we could've been in trouble.

372
00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:17.400
His body was like a big mass of goo
in there. It didn't have a real shape.

373
00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.930
So he was like a pile of mud?

374
00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:22.070
[FRANKY]
Yeah, if I had to guess,
it's a devil fruit power.

375
00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:24.740
Most likely a Logia-type
fruit at that.

376
00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:26.920
He was giving us a false
sense of security,

377
00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:28.850
'cause he could've
escaped at any time.

378
00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:31.660
[CARIBOU]
Get me outta here!
I'll behave, I swear!

379
00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.080
You, in the banana hammock!

380
00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:35.620
If you let me out,
I'll be your servant!

381
00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:36.970
Come on!

382
00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:41.780
Hm? You feelin' all
right, Chopper?

383
00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:45.320
I dunno. It just
got really hot.

384
00:18:45.320 --> 00:18:48.900
I can't stand the heat. I'm dying.

385
00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:51.380
Sheesh! It is warmer!

386
00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:53.300
[dramatic orchestral music]

387
00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.230
Uh! Wait a second.
Is that smoke?

388
00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.530
We can't see what's
in front of us through that!

389
00:18:58.100 --> 00:19:01.070
Smoke underwater? Can't be.

390
00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.640
Actually, it can.

391
00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:04.910
Is that...?

392
00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.020
Hydrothermal deposits!

393
00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:12.950
What?

394
00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.520
Keep up! This is
a volcanic area!

395
00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:16.490
For real?

396
00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:17.820
[NAMI]
Yes, for real!

397
00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.960
You can see where
there've been eruptions!

398
00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.830
[FRANKY]
We have to get outta here, now!

399
00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:24.960
If one of those erupts,
we're as good as dead!

400
00:19:24.960 --> 00:19:27.930
It's hot. I'm so hot.

401
00:19:30.630 --> 00:19:32.470
[CHOPPER]
There's something coming after us!

402
00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:34.300
It's carnivorous tubeworms!

403
00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:35.610
Got no choice.

404
00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:38.380
Small one. Coup de Burst!

405
00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:41.980
[BOTH scream]

406
00:19:42.010 --> 00:19:44.280
[BROOK]
Faceless crabs!

407
00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:46.520
[FRANKY]
Have to risk it again.
Coup de Burst!

408
00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:47.950
[ALL scream]

409
00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:50.050
[USOPP]
I don't even know what
the hell those things are!

410
00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:52.990
Hang on, guys! Coup de Burst!

411
00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.830
[CHOPPER]
The sea is awful! I hate it!

412
00:19:55.830 --> 00:20:00.160
There's no way the others can
survive down here on their own.

413
00:20:00.160 --> 00:20:01.970
I can't believe
this is happening.

414
00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.900
And we'd only just
gotten back together.

415
00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:07.500
Stop crying! Those three
are way too tough to die!

416
00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:10.410
Even using the Coup
de Burst that sparingly,

417
00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:13.980
we've lost so much air already!

418
00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.010
Huh?

419
00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:19.650
What is that? A light
in the darkness?

420
00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:22.320
Wait, is that Fishman Island?

421
00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:24.350
Maybe Luffy beat us there!

422
00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:27.390
It can't be. We haven't
descended the last 3,000 meters.

423
00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:30.160
"Who are you? A friend?"

424
00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.390
Stop!

425
00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:34.500
If you wanna flash signals,
do it without actually flashing!

426
00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:35.570
Can you tell what it is?

427
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.300
[tense orchestral music]

428
00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:37.950
[CHOPPER]
No, it's still too bright to see.

429
00:20:40.040 --> 00:20:41.910
[gasps] Oh, no!

430
00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.240
An anglerfish! We're screwed!

431
00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:48.380
[CHOPPER screams]

432
00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:51.850
The deep-sea hunter fooled us,
hook, line, and sinker!

433
00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:56.450
[USOPP]
Uh! A little close that time!

434
00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:58.960
There isn't anywhere
left for us to run.

435
00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:00.520
What can we do?

436
00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:03.530
[screams]

437
00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.830
[whimpering]

438
00:21:06.860 --> 00:21:08.600
This can't be happening!

439
00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:10.030
It's human?

440
00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:12.070
No! This doesn't make any sense!

441
00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:17.370
A sea monster... that's
taken on the form of a man!

442
00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:21.780
It's a sea bonze!

443
00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.680
[CHOPPER]
Ah! He's gonna capsize the ship!

444
00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.550
[ALL screaming]

445
00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:31.920
What the...?

446
00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:33.530
Hey, that's naughty!

447
00:21:33.530 --> 00:21:36.380
You know better, Ankoro! Ugh.

448
00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:38.680
You're not allowed to eat ships!

449
00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:42.340
How many times do
I have to tell you?

450
00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:45.710
Captain Vander Decken won't be
happy when he hears about this.

451
00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.980
Wait. Did he just help us?

452
00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.180
Who freakin' cares?

453
00:21:50.180 --> 00:21:53.690
Let's just make a break for it!
He might change his mind!

454
00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:59.550
[DECKEN exhales, then inhales]

455
00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:03.630
[VANDER DECKEN singing]
♪ Dead men tell no tales,
and dead men have no needs...

456
00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:05.350
[BROOK]
Is that me?

457
00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:08.060
[VANDER DECKEN]
I pluck the rings
right off their hands

458
00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.300
[ominous music]

459
00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:11.000
within these shadowy seas.

460
00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:16.050
Dead men have no regrets
and no tears left to weep.

461
00:22:16.080 --> 00:22:18.890
I'll pluck the crowns
right off their heads

462
00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:21.790
within this cold, black deep.

463
00:22:21.820 --> 00:22:24.690
Sunken treasures
free for the taking!

464
00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:27.330
A king of pirates in the making!

465
00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:31.300
I leave my enemies,
weeping and shaking!

466
00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:36.300
Vander Decken is my name,
and these long-lost riches

467
00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:38.410
I do claim! ♪

468
00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.870
[FLYING PIRATES cheer]

469
00:22:40.910 --> 00:22:43.780
[screams] Go away!

470
00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:47.300
[dramatic brass music]

471
00:22:46.180 --> 00:22:48.750
[gasps] No, it can't be!

472
00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:53.300
[CHOPPER whimpers]

473
00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:57.060
[screams] It's a ghost ship!

474
00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:00.000
You are the last one
who should be scared!

475
00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.700
You can't get with these
moves! Whoo!

476
00:23:03.560 --> 00:23:05.070
Tell us that thing isn't real!

477
00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:06.850
Tell us it's like your ship!

478
00:23:06.850 --> 00:23:11.330
Nothing would make me happier,
but take a look at their sail!

479
00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:12.300
[ominous string music]

480
00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:14.680
That's the legendary
Flying Dutchman!

481
00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:17.800
It shouldn't be here!
It shouldn't exist!

482
00:23:17.800 --> 00:23:22.370
As the story goes, it sailed
the seas hundreds of years ago.

483
00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:24.400
One dark and stormy night,

484
00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:27.540
the captain of the ship
suddenly lost his mind.

485
00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:30.510
Consumed with madness,
he threw his own crewmates

486
00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:32.810
into the sea, one after another.

487
00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:36.850
Then, he turned his gaze to the
heavens and cursed the very gods!

488
00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:40.190
The captain's name was none
other than Vander Decken,

489
00:23:40.190 --> 00:23:42.430
and the ship was
the Flying Dutchman.

490
00:23:42.430 --> 00:23:45.450
The gods condemned
him for his actions,

491
00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:48.220
and he was cursed
for all eternity.

492
00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:52.240
Sailing the seas aimlessly,
there on that very vessel!

493
00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:54.020
[BROOK]
Even if you're a skeleton
who has sailed

494
00:23:54.020 --> 00:23:56.860
on a ghost ship of your own,
the sight of the Flying Dutchman

495
00:23:56.860 --> 00:23:59.500
will put chills down your spine!

496
00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:03.080
[DECKEN]
Listen up, I'm not
digging their treasure

497
00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.530
out of your stomachs,
so no eating the ship!

498
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:07.300
[urgent orchestral music]

499
00:24:05.890 --> 00:24:08.230
Just give it a good knock!

500
00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:11.220
You betcha!

501
00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:13.430
[USOPP]
I think we're about to get pounded!

502
00:24:13.430 --> 00:24:15.450
[CHOPPER]
Well, sure! He's our enemy!

503
00:24:15.450 --> 00:24:17.790
Franky, we need
a Coup de Burst! Now!

504
00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:20.700
[FRANKY]
I can't! We used up
all our fuel already!

505
00:24:20.700 --> 00:24:23.820
That means we're on our own till
I can restock the cola supply!

506
00:24:23.830 --> 00:24:25.630
[WADATSUMI yells]

507
00:24:25.640 --> 00:24:27.440
[BOTH scream]

508
00:24:27.450 --> 00:24:29.160
Do something!

509
00:24:29.160 --> 00:24:30.570
Help me!

510
00:24:30.570 --> 00:24:32.080
We're dead!

511
00:24:38.220 --> 00:24:41.590
[grunting]

512
00:24:41.600 --> 00:24:45.400
[STRAW HATS yelling]

513
00:24:45.410 --> 00:24:46.910
What?!

514
00:24:52.080 --> 00:24:55.180
That's the Monster
of the Arctic, the Kraken.

515
00:25:04.850 --> 00:25:08.320
[LUFFY]
All right, he learned
his lesson. Enough!

516
00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:12.300
[triumphant orchestral music]

517
00:25:14.360 --> 00:25:15.660
[LUFFY]
Good boy!

518
00:25:17.660 --> 00:25:20.000
[LUFFY]
Hey!

519
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.360
– [ALL cheer]
– [USOPP] Guys!

520
00:25:21.360 --> 00:25:23.230
I thought you were dead!

521
00:25:23.230 --> 00:25:26.000
That was so scary!

522
00:25:25.000 --> 00:25:27.300
[lighthearted music]

523
00:25:26.000 --> 00:25:28.100
What the heck happened to you?

524
00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:31.840
Nami-swan! Robin!

525
00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:35.340
It was crazy, that's for sure!

526
00:25:35.340 --> 00:25:37.950
They got lost. Morons.

527
00:25:37.950 --> 00:25:39.880
They're hopeless without me.

528
00:25:40.240 --> 00:25:42.720
You gonna take that, Wadatsumi?

529
00:25:42.720 --> 00:25:45.100
Get back up! Avenge yourself!

530
00:25:45.100 --> 00:25:46.530
Start swinging!

531
00:25:46.540 --> 00:25:49.210
[WADATSUMI groans]

532
00:25:49.220 --> 00:25:51.300
[LUFFY]
My bubble popped
and so did Sanji's,

533
00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:55.980
so we all had to crowd inside
Zoro's before we drowned!

534
00:25:55.980 --> 00:25:57.490
We were running outta air!

535
00:25:57.490 --> 00:25:59.740
How 'bout you stop
scaring us like that?

536
00:25:59.740 --> 00:26:01.980
Now a song for you, Captain.

537
00:26:01.980 --> 00:26:05.690
[LUFFY sighs]
Finally! I can stretch my legs!

538
00:26:05.690 --> 00:26:06.920
[CHOPPER]
Luffy!

539
00:26:06.920 --> 00:26:09.320
We thought you
were gone forever!

540
00:26:09.350 --> 00:26:10.520
[sobs]

541
00:26:10.550 --> 00:26:13.190
If you survived that,
you can survive anything!

542
00:26:13.190 --> 00:26:15.360
No kidding,
and you tamed the Kraken

543
00:26:15.360 --> 00:26:18.670
just like you said.
I thought you were nuts!

544
00:26:18.670 --> 00:26:21.770
[ROBIN laughs] So, is he
going to be our new guide?

545
00:26:21.770 --> 00:26:22.980
Yeah!

546
00:26:22.980 --> 00:26:25.040
If that goopy dude can have
a sea monster pull his ship,

547
00:26:25.040 --> 00:26:27.010
then we can have
Surume pull the Sunny.

548
00:26:27.010 --> 00:26:28.250
Right, pal?

549
00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:30.620
[USOPP]
Of course, you would name
it already, wouldn't you?

550
00:26:30.620 --> 00:26:33.920
[BROOK singing]
♪ Surume!

551
00:26:33.920 --> 00:26:35.890
♪ I think our captain's insane
to give it such a name, ♪

552
00:26:35.890 --> 00:26:38.020
♪ but as long as it can
carry us, I won't complain! ♪

553
00:26:38.020 --> 00:26:41.260
Now, pull the Sunny
forward. Let's go!

554
00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:44.800
[USOPP]
Uh, that's cool if he wants
to give us a free ride.

555
00:26:44.800 --> 00:26:48.100
But make sure he doesn't crush
us with those giant tentacles.

556
00:26:48.100 --> 00:26:50.540
[FLYING PIRATE]
Captain, the ship's getting away.

557
00:26:50.540 --> 00:26:52.610
[DECKEN]
You think I can't see the Kraken?

558
00:26:52.610 --> 00:26:53.640
Follow them!

559
00:26:53.640 --> 00:26:55.370
[FLYING PIRATES]
– Aye, aye!
– Aye, aye!

560
00:26:56.890 --> 00:26:59.050
[PIRATES gasp]

561
00:26:59.090 --> 00:27:00.860
What's that?

562
00:27:06.150 --> 00:27:07.400
Captain, stop!

563
00:27:07.400 --> 00:27:10.130
We gotta turn back,
or we're dead!

564
00:27:13.090 --> 00:27:16.880
I knew it. An undersea
volcano. Straight ahead.

565
00:27:16.880 --> 00:27:19.520
[USOPP, CHOPPER, BROOK, FRANKY]
– What?
– What?

566
00:27:18.900 --> 00:27:21.100
[BE:FIRST singing "Sailing"]
